<title>USA: CCC seeks up to 30,000 T U.S. HRW wheat for Bosnia.</title>
<headline>CCC seeks up to 30,000 T U.S. HRW wheat for Bosnia.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commodity Credit Corp said it would seek up to 30,000 tonnes of U.S. No. 2 or better hard red winter wheat under its export donation program to Bosnia.</p>
<p>The shipment period was slated for January 25-February 20.</p>
<p>The wheat must originate in areas of the United States where Tilletia Indica (Karnal Bunt) is not known to occur.</p>
<p>Offers were due January 7.</p>
<p>The CCC is part of the U.S. Department of Agriculture.</p>
<p>((Doris Frankel 312-983-7305))</p>
